A||||15||pHoOl||Crying after a race||||1||
Z||000000||pHoOl||01-18-2001||01:31 AM||||Alrighty, so me and my roommate go out with his girlfriend and her roommate tonight.  She's driving a cavalier, pretty new looking.  I think it was a Z24 due to the monochrome body panals and such.  At least i really hope that it was a 24.  Anyway... to make a long story short, we're side by side at a light.  I joke around about racing, and she says no way since i'm in a fiero and she's in a cavalier.  I don't know whether i didn't have it floored or what, but we both launched and she stayed even with me up until 45 when i just shut down to avoid speeding.  <P>Any thoughts on this?  I hear about guys racing mustangs in their GTs and it kinda depresses me that i had a cavalier keeping up with me.  Thanks for the time and bandwidth.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||01-18-2001||01:42 AM||||I wouldnt worry about it too much. Ive had Mustangs in my rear view mirror and Volvos pulling away from me. Some days are just better than others I think. Maybe its just me, but cars these days really seem to pack alot more punch then they did in the past.....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||01-18-2001||03:00 AM||||Last race I had was against I newer Dodge Ram 1500 V8.. don't know if it was modded or not but the guy had an NHRA sticker in the back window  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Took him by a nose up to 80.. not bad for my GT with 154,000 miles on it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The guy was really cool, too.  Gave me a big thumbs up and lots of grins.  It's great that there's people that like cars no matter what they are..<P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: Standard88||||reg||
Z||000003||Cheever2||01-18-2001||03:23 AM||||THERE'S NO CRYING IN RACING!!!<P>eh-hem... I heard that tow truck drivers will race anybody.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000004||GT Bastard||01-18-2001||08:22 AM||||I lined up to a newish 3800 Buick last summer, and some chicks were driving.  I thought they were trying to race me for laughs, so I humored them by taking off quickly(not really launching hard) from the light.  Well, they hammered it and blew past me.  By the time I hit it full throttle, it was too late to catch up.  I was like, "uhh... I hope nobody saw that."||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLisa||01-18-2001||10:24 AM||||Oh no, how about this:  a HEARSE tried to race me. or should I say did race me. And beat me. How embarrasing is that, some big big guy and (probably, hopefully) his daughter pulled up beside me at this light, and I'm just like, fine, I'll play along. Wow it was entirely too close- He had more top end, ya know, important to transport those bodies fast!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||TheFiero64||01-18-2001||11:03 AM||||I got blown away by a tarus SHO last summer <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||01-18-2001||11:49 AM||||I wasted a contour v-6 today up a short straight entrance ramp. I must have had 3 car lengths on it by the time I hit 55mph. The driver was trying to race me too.||||reg||1
Z||000008||sqoach||01-18-2001||01:22 PM||||phool, don't feel bad about that. those z24 cav's are pretty damn quick. my friend's mom has one and it has some power. unless it wasn't a z24, then...hahahaha you suck!<BR>j/k  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>probably was though. remember those newer cars have a lot less miles which means their engines are a lot cleaner and can run smoother. when i got some new stuff for my engine, i.e. plugs, distributor cap, etc., it ran a lot better. i beat my friend's 96 civic too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (up to about 50, that is)||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||01-18-2001||05:38 PM||||My truck could blow the doors off my 5-speed formula on the highway! It is a two wheel drive Toyota Tundra with the 32 valve I-force V8 engine. That thing halls.||||reg||1
Z||000010||pHoOl||01-19-2001||02:42 AM||||yeah, i'm thinking that i'll try replacing plugs as soon as it gets warm out.  i'm not sure if the previous owner replace the back ones since they're kinda hard to get to from what i'm told.  beats me, but it's almost a year that i've had it, and this spring is cleaning time.  hopefully take the seats out and clean carpet all the way around.  anyway......<P>umm, how much does getting an engine rebuilt help?  from what i understand its' kinda like getting a new engine.  forgive my ignorence.  Hmm, another question, how hard and how beneficial is replacing the spark plug wires?  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||danny boy||01-20-2001||01:10 AM|||| Dont feel bad, I got beat by a minivan.||||reg||8
Z||000012||Formula88||02-18-2001||02:26 AM||||Hey, FieroLisa, don't worry about losing to a Hearse.  Most of those started life as an ambulance and have serious engines in them! The old Cadillac Hearst's are known for having upwards of 500 cubes and almost 400 HP!  Newer ones are probably closer to an average Police car in terms of power.  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||lou_dias||02-18-2001||05:41 PM||||Z24'a are fairly quick and generally keep up with mustangs (stock) pretty good as long as they have the 5speed.  They weigh about the same as Fiero GT's and if they have the 3.1 in them then they also have 20 more horses + torque.<P>I drove a friend's stock 5speed 3.1 Cavalier with an aftermarket muffler and I still beleive it pulled harder than my rebuilt 3.4 with performance parts.  This goes back to my statements on long-ago threads that MFI sucks and we need SFI, roller cams and aluminum heads to truly realize the potential of the v6-60 degree motor in our babies. Remember air+fuel going out is never greater that than air going in. In other words, the more you put in, the more comes out.<P>If you want more performance, start getting more air into your engine first.  Their are more rewards there than doing an exhaust first.  Don't believe the (exhaust) hype.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Standard||02-18-2001||11:42 PM||||I'm pretty sure that SFI goes back to batch fire like MPFI after 3,000 rpm.  The biggest advantage the FWD's have is the aluminum heads.  They flow much better than the iron ones, and the combustion chamber is a much better shape.  Half a hemi, pretty much.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Formula88||02-20-2001||12:43 PM||||Has anyone checked into the current 3400SFI V6 for a swap?  It's rated at about 170hp (depending on application) and about 200ft-lbs of torque.  I've got on in my 99 Grand Am and it is a sweet engine.  It runs almost dead even with LZeitgeist's 88 Formula 5-speed, and the GA is an automatic.  With a few speed parts, it could be a great engine in a Fiero.  Solid, smooth, and reliable, too.  Next up would have to be the 3.4TDC.  Ram Air Technology is putting together a kit for a 40hp improvement on it, so it would be pushing more hp than a stock 3800SC!  Not as much torque, though, but that could help the longevity of the drivetrain.  Any ideas?  <P>Check out: <A HREF="http://www.ramairtech.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ramairtech.com</A> <BR>           <A HREF="http://www.twindualcam.com" TARGET=_blank>www.twindualcam.com</A> <BR>for more info.||||reg||6
